From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: log query pools the host driver refuses

Venus creates query pools asynchronously (vn_async_vkCreateQueryPool): a pool
the driver refuses stays unknown to vkr, and the guest's first
vkCmdResetQueryPool / vkCmdBeginQuery / vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults on it is a
fatal CS error that kills the application's GPU context, after which the game
waits forever on fences that never signal.  STEAMAC-2X (Path of Exile 2 on
KosmicKrisp, M3, 1.9): "failed to look up object 4574 of type 12",
"vkCmdResetQueryPool resulted in CS error" five seconds after the game window
appeared, the same id on both launches, then an endless loading screen with
the GPU idle.  Nothing named the refused pool: KosmicKrisp's vk_errorf reasons
are not printed in release builds.

vkCreateQueryPool now logs a refused pool with the driver's VkResult, its id
(the one the CS error later names) and its create info (query type, count,
pipeline statistics, flags, whether a pNext chain was given).
---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_query_pool.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_query_pool.c
@@ -7,11 +7,27 @@
 
 #include "vkr_query_pool_gen.h"
 
+/* Venus creates query pools asynchronously: when the driver refuses one, the guest still
+ * holds its id and the first command buffer resetting, beginning or copying it is a fatal
+ * CS error ("failed to look up object N of type 12") that kills the application's GPU
+ * context. Name the refused pool so that report says why.
+ */
 static void
 vkr_dispatch_vkCreateQueryPool(struct vn_dispatch_context *dispatch,
                                struct vn_command_vkCreateQueryPool *args)
 {
-   vkr_query_pool_create_and_add(dispatch->data, args);
+   if (vkr_query_pool_create_and_add(dispatch->data, args) || !args->pCreateInfo ||
+       !args->pQueryPool)
+      return;
+
+   const VkQueryPoolCreateInfo *info = args->pCreateInfo;
+   vkr_log("vkCreateQueryPool failed on the host (VkResult %d): query pool %" PRIu64
+           " (type %d, %u queries, statistics 0x%x, flags 0x%x%s) is unknown, commands using "
+           "it are CS errors",
+           args->ret,
+           vkr_cs_handle_load_id((const void **)args->pQueryPool, VK_OBJECT_TYPE_QUERY_POOL),
+           info->queryType, info->queryCount, info->pipelineStatistics, info->flags,
+           info->pNext ? ", with pNext" : "");
 }
 
 static void
